    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Summer 1990. Three unconventional characters have settled in Campbellton, a small town on the border between New Brunswick and the Gaspé Peninsula. They are ugly, different from others, and possibly even venomous… like platypuses. Twelve-year-old Sardine is finding early adolescence difficult, what with the shenanigans of her Uncle Steeve (a charming junkie) and her friend Guillaume’s desperate attempts to please men. Together they form a strange trio, an odd patchwork family. \n\nYears later, the three meet up again and try to..."
      }
    ],
